WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.310
Bergmann built one of Europe's premier protein laboratories inside a leather

2
00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:11.650
research institute because leather is collagen, and collagen is protein.

3
00:00:12.483 --> 00:00:17.843
Then in 1933 the Nazi state expelled him for being Jewish, and he rebuilt at

4
00:00:17.843 --> 00:00:22.683
Rockefeller, carrying the carbobenzoxy-protecting group chemistry and a conviction

5
00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:27.243
most chemists did not yet share: that proteins had readable sequences.

6
00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:32.847
But a sequence could not be read, he was certain, until its alphabet had first been

7
00:00:32.847 --> 00:00:37.927
counted, so he set new recruits to the unglamorous arithmetic of naming every amino

8
00:00:37.927 --> 00:00:40.227
acid in a protein and in what amount.

9
00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:46.037
He framed it in terms they did not forget the amino acid analysis of proteins, he

10
00:00:46.037 --> 00:00:50.217
told them, bore the same relationship to these macromolecules that elementary

11
00:00:50.217 --> 00:00:54.057
analysis bore to the chemistry of simpler organic substances.

12
00:00:54.817 --> 00:01:00.057
When Moore arrived in 1939 he found Stein already at the bench, and Bergmann told

13
00:01:00.057 --> 00:01:01.377
them to combine their efforts.

14
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.120
Bergmann died in 1944, before Sanger's insulin sequence proved him right.

15
00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.740
The quiet lab his two recruits inherited went on to win the Nobel he did not live to

16
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:13.020
share.
